Below is one possible patch to let the GeoTIFF source honour a user‐supplied projection (so that WebGLTileLayer can pick up the source’s native CRS and reprojection will “just work”). In your repro you were passing  

```js
new ol.source.GeoTIFF({
  sources: […],
  // projection: cogProj
});
```

but the constructor was unconditionally calling `super(..., projection: null, …)`, so your `projection` option was simply dropped. Changing that to use `options.projection` restores the ability for DataTile (and WebGLTileLayer) to reprojection automatically.

```javascript
### src/ol/source/GeoTIFF.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
    constructor(options) {
      super({
        state: 'loading',
        tileGrid: null,
        projection: null,
        opaque: options.opaque,
        transition: options.transition,
        interpolate: options.interpolate !== false,
        wrapX: options.wrapX,
      });
>>>>>>> SEARCH
